package com.enil.logez.core.designsystem

import com.enil.logez.core.domain.model.MuscleGroup

/**
 * Raw geometry backing [BodyDiagram] -- SVG path ("d" attribute) data adapted from
 * **vue-human-muscle-anatomy** by Luca Wahlen (MIT License). The original
 * `LucaWahlen/vue-human-muscle-anatomy` GitHub repository has been deleted; this data was fetched
 * 2026-09-22 from the `sebmaynard/vue-human-muscle-anatomy` fork
 * (github.com/sebmaynard/vue-human-muscle-anatomy), whose `LICENSE` file confirms MIT,
 * Copyright (c) 2025 Luca Wahlen. Used under the MIT terms, with the notice shipped on the
 * Open-source licences screen. Replaces the prior vulovix/body-muscles (Apache-2.0) data.
 *
 * Unlike the prior data, front and back are already combined in ONE shared
 * [MUSCLE_BODY_VIEW_BOX]x[MUSCLE_BODY_VIEW_BOX] coordinate space per gender (front figure roughly
 * `x<512`, back roughly `x>=512`, confirmed by each path's own bounding box) -- see
 * [BodyDiagram] for the single-canvas render this enables. There is also only ONE shape per
 * muscle group total (not one per side), so no [MuscleGroup] needs merging across regions the way
 * the prior 89-sub-region data did.
 *
 * The female figure's source paths were `transform="matrix(...)"`-wrapped (some reusing the male
 * figure's own geometry via an axis-aligned translation); those matrices were baked into absolute
 * coordinates once, offline, before this file was generated -- nothing in [BodyDiagram] applies a
 * transform at draw time.
 *
 * Not every source shape maps to a [MuscleGroup] -- `outline-front`/`outline-back` ([group] null)
 * render as unlabeled base-silhouette context only, the same role the prior data's ungrouped
 * regions played.
 *
 * Two mapping approximations, both this integration's own judgment call (documented here the same
 * way the prior data documented its own two): `rotatorCuffs` (the scapular/rotator-cuff mass) ->
 * [MuscleGroup.UPPER_BACK] -- the best available proxy for that group's rhomboid/mid-trap
 * definition, since this asset has no dedicated rhomboid shape; `shins` -> [MuscleGroup.CALVES] --
 * the same lower-leg simplification the prior data also made (there is no separate "shin" group in
 * the app's 20-value enum). `lowerBack` -> [MuscleGroup.LOWER_BACK] is a genuine, unapproximated
 * match -- this asset actually draws it, unlike the previously-shipped data, which had no
 * lower-back geometry at all.
 */
const val MUSCLE_BODY_VIEW_BOX = 1024f

